# The oracle references, pinned.
#
# One line per reference, tab-separated: <name> <image> <version> <what it
# answers>.
#
# **Every line names the same image.** These are not four tools each answering
# about its own format. Blender, f3d and FreeCAD are asked the same question
# about an OBJ, and the whole value is in where they disagree. OpenSCAD does
# not read OBJ in this release; it is in the set so a later format asks the
# same image. In four images with four base states, a disagreement would first
# have to be shown not to be the images' fault. One image makes "the reference
# set" one fact.
#
# The image is built here, so the tag is not a digest of the finished image:
# two builds of one Containerfile are not two copies of one image. What is
# pinned instead is everything the build reads - the base by digest, the
# packages by full apt version, resolved against a dated snapshot of the
# Debian archive so the pins do not expire - and the run-time version check
# is the real guarantee. oracle_env.check_pin() therefore runs in both modes.
# There is no stock image named here, so relaxing the check in host mode would
# leave nothing checking anything.
#
# The tag is Blender, then f3d, then FreeCAD, then OpenSCAD:
# 4.3.2-3.1.0-1.0.0-2021.01. The version field names what decides an answer,
# which for f3d is not f3d. f3d is how VTK's vtkOBJReader is reached, and a
# newer VTK behind the same f3d package is a different reader, so the field
# names both. FreeCAD's field is FreeCAD's own version: the package also
# links VTK, and that is not the code that reads an OBJ.
#
# Raising a pin is deliberate. A new reference version is new answers, and a
# new answer that disagrees is a finding to triage rather than a regression
# to fix.
#
# Building it:
#   make oracle-build

blender	localhost/ghoti-model-oracle-readers:4.3.2-3.1.0-1.0.0-2021.01	Blender 4.3.2	Blender's OBJ importer, and the only reader of the MTL statements VTK declines
f3d	localhost/ghoti-model-oracle-readers:4.3.2-3.1.0-1.0.0-2021.01	F3D 3.1.0, VTK 9.3.0.	vtkOBJReader, reached through f3d because VTK ships no OBJ binary of its own
freecad	localhost/ghoti-model-oracle-readers:4.3.2-3.1.0-1.0.0-2021.01	FreeCAD 1.0.0	FreeCAD's own OBJ reader and writer, ReaderOBJ and WriterOBJ, which also load the MTL
openscad	localhost/ghoti-model-oracle-readers:4.3.2-3.1.0-1.0.0-2021.01	OpenSCAD version 2021.01	CGAL and OpenCSG. This release has no OBJ; it answers STL, OFF, AMF and 3MF when those formats arrive
